cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NurosOS in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "NurosOS: A Bio-Inspired Neuromorphic Operating System Based on the Drosophila Connectome"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "NurosOS Contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/modarresi1913/NurosOS"
repository-code: "https://github.com/modarresi1913/NurosOS"
url: "https://github.com/modarresi1913/NurosOS"
abstract: >
  NurosOS is a next-generation operating system and runtime environment
  architected upon the structural and functional principles derived
  from the complete connectome of Drosophila melanogaster. By translating
  the 125 million synaptic connections and sparse, feedback-driven neural
  topologies into software primitives, NurosOS provides a radical new
  paradigm for energy-efficient, highly parallel, and adaptive computing.
keywords:
  - neuromorphic-computing
  - spiking-neural-networks
  - drosophila-connectome
  - event-driven-operating-system
  - bio-inspired-computing
  - intel-loihi
  - rust
  - synapselang
  - sparse-propagation-protocol
  - associative-memory
